s the driver of negligence and of violating South Carolina traffic laws and federal motor carrier safety rules. The suit also accuses CTS of negligent hiring, retention, training and supervision, seeks actual, consequential and punitive damages, and has requested a jury trial.</description></item><item><title>J. J. Keller urges motor carriers to strengthen cargo security ahead of Thanksgiving</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/j-j-keller-urges-motor-carriers-to-strengthen-cargo-security-ahead-of-358dd7c86a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/j-j-keller-urges-motor-carriers-to-strengthen-cargo-security-ahead-of-358dd7c86a/</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:26:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>American Journal of Transportation</description></item></channel></rss>